# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo and on checkout.
#
# Without this, Windows CI runners (where git's `core.autocrlf=true` is
# the default) check out files with CRLF endings, which then trips the
# `mixed-line-ending` pre-commit hook with `--fix=lf` and fails the
# matrix's Windows leg. With `eol=lf`, .gitattributes overrides
# `core.autocrlf` and forces LF everywhere — same bytes on every OS.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect binary files (PNG, sqlite, etc.) and
# leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
